  "prediction": "The backoff strategies involve using alternative models or approaches when the primary model fails to provide accurate results. In the context of the article, this refers to using a background model as a fallback option when the ScRNN predicts an out-of-vocabulary word. The neutral backoff variant returns a fixed neutral word whenever the ScRNN predicts an UNK, reducing the number of unique outputs it predicts. Open vocabulary models, on the other hand, consider each character combination uniquely, making the pass-through version more sensitive than the background variant for char-only, word+char, and word-",
  "scored_prediction": "The backoff strategies involve using alternative models or approaches when the primary model fails to provide accurate results. In the context of the article, this refers to using a background model as a fallback option when the ScRNN predicts an out-of-vocabulary word. The neutral backoff variant returns a fixed neutral word whenever the ScRNN predicts an UNK, reducing the number of unique outputs it predicts. Open vocabulary models, on the other hand, consider each character combination uniquely, making the pass-through version more sensitive than the background variant for char-only, word+char, and word-",
  "score": 27.659574468085108,
  "answers": [
    "In pass-through, the recognizer passes on the possibly misspelled word, backoff to neutral word backs off to a word with similar distribution across classes and backoff to background model backs off to a more generic word recognition model trained with larger and less specialized corpus.",
